      "nonClaim": "The framer remains paired-input-only and, despite collision-free table concatenation, is not composed with the lifted simulator into one execution: the concatenated table has no bridge rule that launches the simulator from the framer halt. The internal handoff compiled theorem starts from an encoded internal configuration, not ordinary startConfig, has no raw-visible machineOutput or terminal de-tagging, and is not composed with the lifted simulator into one execution; no simulator halt launches the handoff. Bounded padding assumes a represented start and a designated-halting source endpoint; it proves no termination or stuck/timeout/verdict correspondence. There is no complete composed WorkMachine execution, no target-stage boundedDecide or machineOutput preservation, no terminal raw output packer, no external input-size polynomial, and no pipeline RawRefinement/composition theorem or charged/raw class equivalence. Here n is a source-transition count and F a source-transition fuel bound, not input length: only 3 * n is an exact successful work count. This does not establish CNF-SAT in P, NP-completeness, or P = NP."
